{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) AS avg_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) AS p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 3,2",
          "claim": "search's GetRates client spans average about 1650 ms, while rate's server spans for the same calls average about 0.5 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abnormal' AS period, count(*) AS n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) AS p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.1)/1e6,1) AS p10_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.9)/1e6,1) AS p90_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' UNION ALL SELECT 'normal', count(*), round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2), round(quantile_cont(duration,0.1)/1e6,2), round(quantile_cont(duration,0.9)/1e6,2) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates'",
          "claim": "search's GetRates client latency moved from about 0.9 ms (normal p50) to about 1540 ms (abnormal p50), tightly clustered."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "search's other outgoing call to geo stays near normal (~0.5 ms), so the slowdown is confined to the rate path.",
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, round(avg(CASE WHEN p='ab' THEN value END),1) AS ab_avg, round(avg(CASE WHEN p='n' THEN value END),1) AS n_avg FROM (SELECT 'ab' p, * FROM abnormal_metrics_sum UNION ALL SELECT 'n', * FROM normal_metrics_sum) WHERE metric IN ('k8s.pod.network.io','k8s.pod.network.errors','k8s.pod.uptime') AND service_name IN ('search','rate') GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 2,1",
          "claim": "search and rate pods show unchanged network I/O, zero network errors, and no uptime reset, so there is no link-level or restart signal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) AS avg_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.9)/1e6,1) AS p90_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('search.Search/Nearby','HTTP /hotels') GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 2,3",
          "claim": "The slowdown carries from search's Nearby server span (~1650 ms) into frontend's HTTP /hotels server spans (~1640 ms)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Summary:** The user-visible degradation is confined to the `/hotels` path (frontend → search → rate). `search`'s outgoing `rate.Rate/GetRates` calls gained roughly 1.5 s before `rate` received them, while `rate`'s own server spans stayed around 0.5 ms. The fault is classed as `http_slow` at the caller, since the connection is healthy, search's other outgoing calls are unaffected, and no network-level signal appears. Note that `network_delay` on the search→rate link would fit the same timing, but the telemetry has no per-connection network metrics to confirm it. The other small shifts (memcached spans in profile and reservation, roughly 0.1–0.4 ms) are too small to be user-visible, so I did not name them as faults.
